{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require Ofgem price cap for heat networks and no heat costs via service charges",
        "additional_details": "Heat-network customers often cannot choose their supplier or switch networks, yet are outside the existing energy price cap. The Government should require Ofgem to set maximum heat-network prices and ensure costs of supplying and operating heat networks, including maintenance, repair, replacement and upgrades, cannot be shifted into residential service charges or recovered twice.",
        "background": "Require Ofgem to introduce a price cap for domestic heat networks, covering unit and standing charges, and prohibit heat-network supply, operation, maintenance, repair, replacement and upgrade costs from being recovered through residential service charges.",
